{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01177",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.92,
      "end_seconds": 5.89,
      "duration_seconds": 4.97,
      "text": "hi, doctor, I came as soon as they called me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.63,
      "end_seconds": 10.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "come in please sit how can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 10.89,
      "end_seconds": 16.35,
      "duration_seconds": 5.46,
      "text": "Hello, doctor, I came in with them, if that's okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 17.45,
      "end_seconds": 20.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "yes, that's no problem at all. Please sit"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 25.96,
      "end_seconds": 31.48,
      "duration_seconds": 5.52,
      "text": "I wanted to get an itchy patch on my wrist looked at."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 32.25,
      "end_seconds": 35.83,
      "duration_seconds": 3.58,
      "text": "Can you tell me when it first started?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 37.14,
      "end_seconds": 39.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "probably six months yeah"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 40.13,
      "end_seconds": 48.12,
      "duration_seconds": 7.99,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 50.07,
      "end_seconds": 63.92,
      "duration_seconds": 13.85,
      "text": "It happens every other day. My new watch strap definitely sets it off. Pretty mild, if I'm being honest. I get some relief from moisturiser."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 64.77,
      "end_seconds": 66.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.13,
      "text": "Is it accompanied by anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 68.56,
      "end_seconds": 75.87,
      "duration_seconds": 7.31,
      "text": "when it starts I tend to get a bit of redness as well"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 77.5,
      "end_seconds": 81.81,
      "duration_seconds": 4.31,
      "text": "What about dry flaky skin, have you noticed that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.37,
      "end_seconds": 91.35,
      "duration_seconds": 8.98,
      "text": "Yes, um, about the same, three weeks. The bit of redness? That's been for three weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.04,
      "end_seconds": 100.44,
      "duration_seconds": 7.4,
      "text": "Have you had an itchy patch on your wrist before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 101.1,
      "end_seconds": 106.03,
      "duration_seconds": 4.93,
      "text": "A bit, last winter. It settled by itself back then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 107.08,
      "end_seconds": 110.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.32,
      "text": "have you had any blisters, fever or spreading?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 112.06,
      "end_seconds": 115.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "I haven't had blisters, fever or spreading, no"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 117.16,
      "end_seconds": 121.48,
      "duration_seconds": 4.32,
      "text": "Anything with your heart, like skipped beats or fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 122.03,
      "end_seconds": 127.07,
      "duration_seconds": 5.04,
      "text": "my heart's been fine, as far as I know"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 127.95,
      "end_seconds": 131.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "Any problems with your joints or muscles?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 133.04,
      "end_seconds": 134.56,
      "duration_seconds": 1.52,
      "text": "No, nothing there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 143.78,
      "end_seconds": 146.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "do you have any long-term conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 148.28,
      "end_seconds": 158.97,
      "duration_seconds": 10.69,
      "text": "I've had diabetes for about ten years now. I looked a few things up online, and that probably didn't help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.6,
      "end_seconds": 162.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "Tell me your medicines, please."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 164.27,
      "end_seconds": 168.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.57,
      "text": "It's metformin, 500 milligrams, twice a day, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.2,
      "end_seconds": 174.12,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "Let me ask about allergies, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 175.21,
      "end_seconds": 177.61,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "Not to my knowledge, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.46,
      "end_seconds": 188.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 189.76,
      "end_seconds": 191.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.1,
      "text": "no, not at all"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 193.69,
      "end_seconds": 194.64,
      "duration_seconds": 0.95,
      "text": "Any smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 195.6,
      "end_seconds": 198.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "I gave up cigarettes last spring."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.86,
      "end_seconds": 201.82,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "Do you drink alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 203.86,
      "end_seconds": 205.56,
      "duration_seconds": 1.7,
      "text": "Nothing, I'm teetotal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 206.71,
      "end_seconds": 209.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "Do you work outside the home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 211.19,
      "end_seconds": 215.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.88,
      "text": "I'm a hairdresser, on my feet all day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 218.7,
      "end_seconds": 221.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "Okay, do you live by yourself?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 222.88,
      "end_seconds": 227.02,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "No, I share a house with my brother."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 228.48,
      "end_seconds": 229.96,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "Are you active?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 231.04,
      "end_seconds": 234.12,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "I walk the dog every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 249.66,
      "end_seconds": 252.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "I'll just record a few vital signs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 259.86,
      "end_seconds": 262.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "Sit still for a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 276.86,
      "end_seconds": 282.02,
      "duration_seconds": 5.16,
      "text": "Okay: heart rate 70, blood pressure 123 over 72, saturation 99 percent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 287.64,
      "end_seconds": 289.04,
      "duration_seconds": 1.4,
      "text": "Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 290.47,
      "end_seconds": 293.51,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "That's fine, I'll explain it soon."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 296.47,
      "end_seconds": 300.85,
      "duration_seconds": 4.38,
      "text": "Now I'm going to do a short physical check."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 301.55,
      "end_seconds": 302.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.11,
      "text": "That's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 304.14,
      "end_seconds": 305.88,
      "duration_seconds": 1.74,
      "text": "let me feel here"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 316.23,
      "end_seconds": 322.18,
      "duration_seconds": 5.95,
      "text": "there's a neat red patch where the watch strap sits, with a little scaling"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 327.19,
      "end_seconds": 337.67,
      "duration_seconds": 10.48,
      "text": "Thank you, you can get dressed. So, based on the history and the examination, the most likely explanation is mild contact dermatitis from the watch strap."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 338.99,
      "end_seconds": 341.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "What are the odds it's serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 342.74,
      "end_seconds": 371.23,
      "duration_seconds": 28.49,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like mild contact dermatitis from the watch strap. I'll start you on hydrocortisone cream, 1%, once a day, one week. That should help with contact dermatitis. Stop wearing that strap and keep the skin moisturised. One warning sign to remember: it spreads or blisters. In that case don't wait."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 374.86,
      "end_seconds": 377.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "that's fine by me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 381.47,
      "end_seconds": 389.77,
      "duration_seconds": 8.3,
      "text": "I'd like you back if it has not cleared in two weeks. So, that's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 390.82,
      "end_seconds": 394.65,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. Thanks for explaining."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 395.71,
      "end_seconds": 397.1,
      "duration_seconds": 1.39,
      "text": "all the best"
    }
  ]
}